00:16:35.370 --> 00:16:48.619
They've watched an entire story, the story had a beginning, middle, and end, and then there's this little magic moment at the end that she happens to be there and that sends us into the second half of what feels like a two-parter, but really it's a complete restart right?
他们看完了整个故事，故事有开头、中间和结尾，然后最后有一个神奇的小时刻，她碰巧在那里，这让我们进入了感觉像是两人合作的后半部分，但这真的是一个完整的重新开始，对吧？

00:16:48.619 --> 00:16:51.249
It's like we're not going to keep talking about Robin.
就好像我们不会继续谈论罗宾一样。

00:16:51.249 --> 00:16:52.418
We are switching it out.
我们正在把它关掉。

00:16:52.418 --> 00:16:54.659
We are now going to be talking about Victoria.
我们现在要谈论维多利亚。

00:16:54.659 --> 00:16:57.289
There's a magic to that moment and it is the universe.
那一刻有一种魔力，那就是宇宙。

00:16:59.129 --> 00:17:14.657
We might want to do a whole episode on this and I don't want to get too deep in the weeds on this, but I think that one of the reasons that how I met your mother resonates so deeply at such a core almost mythic level with people.
我们可能想用一整集来讨论这个问题，我不想在这个问题上陷得太深，但我认为我遇见你母亲的原因之一在这样一个核心几乎是神话般的层面上与人们产生了如此深刻的共鸣。

00:17:14.657 --> 00:17:34.592
You know, there's a lot of, you know, this is, but like, the history of science and theology, like when the scientific revolution happened and the enlightenment happened and God was kind of plucked out of the center of the universe and it became all about verifiable, provable material reality.
你知道，有很多，你知道，这就像科学和神学的历史，就像当科学革命发生和启蒙运动发生时，上帝被从宇宙中心拉出来，一切都变成了可验证的、可证明的物质现实。

00:17:34.592 --> 00:17:48.356
And there's this ache at the heart of the modern life, which is like, we long for transcendence, we long for, we're still wired to believe in something beyond that, which we can verify or measure, right?
现代生活的核心有一种痛苦，那就是，我们渴望超越，我们渴望，我们仍然相信超越这一点的东西，我们可以验证或衡量，对吗？

00:17:48.356 --> 00:17:57.442
And I think that there's something about how I met your mother, someone could write a really good paper on this, and maybe I'll do it.
我认为我是如何认识你母亲的，有人可以就此写一篇非常好的论文，也许我会这么做。

00:17:57.442 --> 00:18:02.867
But there's something about it puts mystery back at the center of things, right?
但它有些东西让神秘重新回到了事情的中心，对吧？

00:18:02.867 --> 00:18:08.156
It's not about, it's a lot about what you cannot control, what you cannot see.
这不是关于，而是关于你无法控制、你看不到的事情。

00:18:08.156 --> 00:18:13.377
There is some sort of guiding hand that is at play and how I met your mother.
我是如何认识你母亲的，这其中有某种指导之手在起作用。

00:18:13.377 --> 00:18:19.615
And I think it's very satisfying on a soul level to people because we don't want to believe.
我认为这在灵魂层面上对人们来说非常令人满意，因为我们不想相信。

00:18:19.615 --> 00:18:24.904
I find a universe that is just material and when we die, it's just lights out.
我发现一个宇宙只是物质的，当我们死后，它就熄灭了。

00:18:24.904 --> 00:18:27.887
I find that to be brutalizing to the psyche.
我发现这对心灵来说是残酷的。

00:18:27.887 --> 00:18:32.227
I find it to be very difficult to exist in a universe like that.
我发现在这样的宇宙中生存是非常困难的。

00:18:32.227 --> 00:18:35.685
And I don't actually exist in a universe like that.
而我实际上并不存在于那样的宇宙中。

00:18:35.685 --> 00:18:37.719
I believe in something bigger.
我相信更大的事情。

00:18:37.719 --> 00:18:40.567
I don't want to unpack all that right now.
我现在不想解开所有这些。

00:18:40.567 --> 00:18:46.398
But I think that part of the magic of how I make a mother is that there's magic in it.
但我认为我如何成为一名母亲的神奇之处在于它本身就有魔力。

00:18:46.398 --> 00:18:49.450
It allows the universe to be enchanted again.
它让宇宙再次着迷。

00:18:49.450 --> 00:18:52.490
And I think that's very satisfying and relieving to people.
我认为这对人们来说非常令人满意和宽慰。

00:18:52.490 --> 00:18:54.730
Yeah, and I like that a lot.
是的，我非常喜欢这样。

00:18:54.730 --> 00:19:01.650
And at the end of this episode, where Ted is so frenzied and trying to force something into being, something bigger is happening.
在这一集的结尾，泰德如此疯狂并试图强迫某些事情成为现实，更大的事情正在发生。

00:19:01.650 --> 00:19:07.210
At the end of this episode that's going to change his life, Future Ted says exactly that at the end, right?
在这一集将改变他的生活的结尾处，未来的泰德在最后说了同样的话，对吗？

00:19:07.210 --> 00:19:13.609
I just turned out, this sent me in a whole other magical direction I couldn't have known about basically as the ending of that episode.
我只是发现，这把我带到了一个完全不同的神奇方向，我基本上无法知道那一集的结局。

00:19:13.609 --> 00:19:20.457
And it's kind of the humbling realization that there are bigger forces that work in our lives and Ted is constantly right there.
这是一种令人谦卑的认识，我们的生活中有更大的力量在发挥作用，而泰德一直就在那里。

00:19:20.457 --> 00:19:22.971
That's the philosophical question of Ted right?
这就是特德的哲学问题，对吗？

00:19:22.971 --> 00:19:29.764
Can you force into being and you plan into being versus how much do you have to sort of surrender yourself to something larger?
你能否强行实现并计划实现，而你必须在多大程度上屈服于更大的事物？

00:19:29.764 --> 00:19:42.281
There's some larger story happening and there's a there's almost something comforting in surrendering to that right because Ted you're so good in these episodes Josh at being the the motor you play the kind of the frenzy of Ted right?
有一些更大的故事正在发生，而且屈服于这一权利几乎是令人欣慰的，因为泰德，你在这些剧集中表现得非常好，乔什，你扮演了泰德的疯狂角色，对吗？

00:19:42.281 --> 00:19:46.989
There's like so there's a bunch of episodes where you are the motor of this show, right?
好像有很多集你都是这个节目的推动者，对吧？

00:19:46.989 --> 00:19:49.449
You're making, you're forcing this into being.
你正在制造，你正在强迫它成为现实。

00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:53.906
There's so many episodes where that's the drive, and then it's nice.
有很多剧集都是这样的，而且很好。

00:19:53.906 --> 00:19:55.609
It's relieving at the end.
到最后就可以缓解了

00:19:55.609 --> 00:19:57.880
Ted surrenders at the end of that episode.
特德在那集结束时投降了。

00:19:57.880 --> 00:20:05.504
He's sitting there with Barney, and he surrenders his preconception about himself that he's the guy that checks I'm going to have a plus one.
他和巴尼坐在一起，他放弃了对自己的先入之见，认为他是检查我是否会获得加一的人。

00:20:05.504 --> 00:20:06.585
He surrenders Robin.
他投降了罗宾。

00:20:06.585 --> 00:20:07.667
I'm trying too hard.
我太努力了。

00:20:07.667 --> 00:20:09.234
I'm working too hard of this.
我为此太努力了。

00:20:09.234 --> 00:20:13.290
It's a complete moment of surrender, And in that moment, he's given a gift.
这是一个完全投降的时刻，在那一刻，他得到了一份礼物。

00:20:13.289 --> 00:20:14.250
Right, right.
对，对。

00:20:14.250 --> 00:20:26.569
And I think part of the complicated math that you and Carter and the writers were doing was like, when is it time for Ted to have a win versus when is it time for him to just slip on the ice or the banana peel?
我认为你和卡特以及编剧们正在做的复杂数学的一部分就像是，什么时候是泰德获胜的时间，什么时候是他在冰上或香蕉皮上滑倒的时间？

00:20:26.569 --> 00:20:26.809
Yeah.
是的。

00:20:26.809 --> 00:20:27.289
You know?
你知道？

00:20:27.289 --> 00:20:27.609
Yeah.
是的。

00:20:27.609 --> 00:20:32.170
And he always got a win right when I felt like he needed it.
当我觉得他需要胜利时，他总是能取得胜利。

00:20:32.170 --> 00:20:37.049
Like I could feel like, oh, thank God he has some wins here, you know?
就像我感觉，哦，感谢上帝，他在这里取得了一些胜利，你知道吗？

00:20:37.049 --> 00:20:38.569
Sometimes you would say that to us.
有时你会对我们这么说。

00:20:38.569 --> 00:20:42.329
You're like, I'm on Ted to stop getting the shit kicked out of him and it's like, you were right.
你就像，我要求特德停止被踢出他的屎，就像，你是对的。

00:20:42.329 --> 00:20:44.752
Whenever you would say that, it was like, he's right.
每当你这么说的时候，你就会觉得他是对的。

00:20:44.752 --> 00:20:46.809
You're the one inhabiting and embodying that.
你就是那个居住并体现这一点的人。

00:20:46.809 --> 00:20:47.847
You're feeling it.
你感觉到了。

00:20:47.847 --> 00:20:48.827
You are that guy.
你就是那个人。

00:20:48.827 --> 00:20:50.556
You're really living with Ted.
你真的和特德住在一起。

00:20:50.556 --> 00:20:52.170
You're living in Ted's skin.
你生活在泰德的皮肤里。

00:20:52.170 --> 00:20:54.890
And you would often protect Ted in that way.
你经常会以这种方式保护特德。

00:20:54.890 --> 00:20:59.759
Well, you become a little bit of the guardian or the gatekeeper of him.
好吧，你成为他的一点守护者或看门人。

00:20:59.759 --> 00:21:03.189
And I'm like, I know what you guys are doing here.
我想，我知道你们在这里做什么。

00:21:03.189 --> 00:21:18.690
Well, sometimes it was like, I wanted less comedy at Ted's expense and more, we'll get into this and I remember feeling it very strongly after drum roll, which is the episode right after, which is zip, zip, zip, is that right?
好吧，有时就像，我想要更少的喜剧，以泰德为代价，更多，我们会进入这个，我记得在击鼓之后感觉非常强烈，这是紧随其后的一集，这是拉链，拉链，拉链，是吗？

00:21:18.690 --> 00:21:19.690
Yeah.
是的。

00:21:19.690 --> 00:21:20.690
Yeah.
是的。

00:21:20.690 --> 00:21:32.849
I remember he's, his romanticism is lionized and heralded in drum roll, please, and then absolutely completely mocked in the next episode and I remember getting whiplash going between the two.
我记得他的浪漫主义被推崇并在鼓声中得到宣扬，然后在下一集中完全被嘲笑，我记得两人之间发生了激烈的冲突。

00:21:32.849 --> 00:21:34.410
I was like, look, is this cute?
我当时想，你看，这可爱吗？

00:21:34.410 --> 00:21:39.730
Do you feel that this is a virtue of his or do you think you wanna mock this?
你觉得这是他的优点还是你想嘲笑他？

00:21:39.730 --> 00:21:41.970
Like I was really confused about it.
就像我真的很困惑一样。

00:21:41.970 --> 00:21:50.970
Yeah, yeah, in such close proximity too because in general, please is such a freaking hero moment for Ted and yeah, yeah, that's interesting.
是的，是的，距离也如此之近，因为总的来说，“拜托”对特德来说是一个英雄般的时刻，是的，是的，这很有趣。

00:21:50.970 --> 00:21:51.809
Well, we'll get there.
好吧，我们会到达那里。

00:21:51.809 --> 00:21:53.970
Well, and we'll untie that when we get there.
好吧，当我们到达那里时，我们会解开这个束缚。

